'pragmat'title="squaring numbers".
$ On the JS target, 46340^2 fits in a signed word and 46341^2 wraps.
'a'intro:
   printf+"Type a number; I will compute its square.%n"
          "To quit, hit Ctrl+D or type a non-number%n".
'p'square and print-n-nn:
   get int+STDIN+n,mult+n+n+nn,
     printf+"the square of %d is %d%n"+n+nn.
$ After a number is read and printed, :nxt repeats the block.
$ If reading fails, the + alternative succeeds and ends the loop.
'root'intro,(nxt:square and print,:nxt;+).
'end'
